WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.396
Planets around other stars.

00:03.096 --> 00:12.442
{exoplanet_count} planets around other stars, in the copy of NASA's catalogue this map carries, each drawn as a mark at its star.

00:12.892 --> 00:21.657
Most were found by the dip in a star's light as a planet crosses in front of it, the rest mostly by the wobble a planet gives its star.
